These are some simple examples of Lattice C++ in action.

To compile them, for each program, the command is:

CC -L program-name.cp

The "-L" option causes the program to be linked after compiling.  Use the
option "-Lm" for the complex arithemetic examples; the 'm' invokes
the floating-point math library.

The examples which use Intuition facilities take a few minutes to compile -
even at 3000 lines per minute, the Intuition headers take a while to
process, and with QUAD: Assigned to RAM:, it might appear as though the
machine had stalled.  Have patience.  Try running the PM program supplied
on your Amiga Extras disk - you'd be suprised at what's going on!

